  "implementation": [
    "Fresh before/after-callback authority checks and pre-KILL escalation check.",
    "Post-fork SpawnAttempt retains OwnedProcess on every launch failure; execution authority is never substituted for cleanup.",
    "One lazy shared service recovery slot bounded by original hard ceiling; deferred observation helpers finish after cancellation and before restoration; incomplete/expired accounting stays sticky.",
    "Detached intermediate and grandchild identities/barriers/status survive handshake errors; pre-exec kernel observation retains fork uncertainty; successful restored stdio remains /dev/null.",
    "Native capture preserves original absolute prelaunch deadline through setup and creation; callback overrun cannot renew phase.",
    "Stopped roots require terminal SIGCHLD and zombie metadata before final reap; all-zombie group required."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Initial TERM/helper baseline probe flaws are disclosed in before-summary.json; only revised service probes establish those failures.",
    "Detached baseline proves missing accounting, not backend exec. After tests separately cover executed actor failure and successful null-stdio/session launch.",
    "Native capture setup tests supplied no lease, runtime, model, production authority or native collector; no inference process could launch.",
    "New CLI cases hit insufficient lifetime-observation budget, not elapsed deadline. Actual expiry is exercised by focused regressions.",
    "First after-run failed stopped-child settlement and exceeded test cleanup ceiling; independent exact-identity test-harness residue disposal is retained in failed-after-owned-residue.json. It is not renewed automation authority or passing settlement evidence.",
    "PID71080 was observed absent after manual disposal using targeted ps (exit1, empty output).",
    "Checks are focused correction evidence, not the historical188-test b576449 result or a full-suite rerun.",
    "No live service control/probes, launchd fixture, selected-runtime reprobe, sensitive reads, native imports/models, shared GPU lease, scheduling, deployment or merge.",
    "G1/G2/G3 remain mandatory; X2/X3 remain unapproved and uninvoked; no retired output-retention gate.",
    "External identity/signal checks remain non-atomic; stalled syscalls have no hard cancellation guarantee; fork uncertainty cannot establish arbitrary-descendant absence.",
    "Actual native endpoint compatibility and restoration fidelity remain unverified; issues11/12 remain open.",
    "Retained CPU authorization files are historical consumed/expired evidence, not reusable grants."
  ],
